### Attribution Platform — Auth endpoints
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "email": "test@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### Get current user (protected) — uses token from the login response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### --- Negative cases ---

### Register with short password (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bad",
  "email": "bad@test.com",
  "password": "short"
}

### Login with wrong password (expect 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@test.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### Access /me without token (expect 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
